.TH WRIKERY 1 2026-10-24 wrikery "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wrikery \- an unofficial terminal client for Wrike
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wrikery
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B wrikery
.RI [ flags ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.br
.B wrikery help
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
wrikery is a terminal client for Wrike, made for people who prefer the keyboard and the terminal over the web application.
It browses the spaces, projects and folders you follow, shows a task with its description, comments, subtasks and dependencies, adds comments, changes statuses, logs time and shows your timesheet, without leaving the terminal.
.PP
It keeps a local copy of what you follow in one SQLite file, so browsing and search are instant and reading works offline.
A change is applied to that copy at once and waits in a queue, which is sent when Wrike can be reached.
The changes screen, !, lists what went out over the last thirty days with the old and the new values, and the writes that failed, for a retry or a discard.
.PP
Without a command it opens the interface.
With a command it runs one operation on the same local copy and exits, for scripts and agents, with \-\-json for a script.
wrikery \-\-demo runs on built in sample data with no account and no network.
The first run asks for a permanent API token, or signs in through the browser when the config file names an API app, and keeps the credential in the system keychain.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-config " PATH
read the config file at PATH instead of the default
.TP
.B \-\-demo
run on built in sample data, no token and no network
.TP
.B \-\-logout
sign out, remove the stored token or session, and exit
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
plain output without colors, NO_COLOR in the environment does the same
.TP
.B \-\-offline
start without syncing, nothing is pulled or sent, R in the interface goes online, wins over offline in the config
.TP
.B \-\-version
print the version and exit
.SH COMMANDS
A task or folder is an id or a part of its title that matches exactly one cached row.
A task may also be the number or the link from the browser, a bare number is always the number from the link, the link in quotes, like "https://app\-eu.wrike.com/open.htm?id=4552825748".
A person is me, a contact id or a part of a name that matches exactly one contact.
A description is markdown, the text the E editor in the interface writes.
The ui commands act on the interface that is running and print what it did, wrikery \-\-demo ui ... drives a demo.
Every command takes \-\-json. Exit codes: 0 done, 1 error, 2 usage, 3 queued but not on Wrike yet.
.SS sync
.B "wrikery sync [\-\-full]"
.PP
Runs one sync cycle, queued writes first, then the pulls, and exits. Ctrl\-C stops it.
\-\-full also checks for tasks deleted on Wrike, which crawls every followed scope and is slower.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-full
also check for tasks deleted on Wrike, slower
.TP
.B \-\-json
print JSON
.RE
.SS The task commands
The task commands read the local cache and queue their writes through the same outbox as the interface.
.SS task list
.B "wrikery task list [\-\-folder F | \-\-me] [\-\-all]"
.PP
Lists open tasks, your own unless \-\-folder names a folder, project or space.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-all
include completed and cancelled tasks
.TP
.BI "\-\-folder " F
F, a folder, project or space, by id or by a part of its title
.TP
.B \-\-json
print JSON
.TP
.B \-\-me
your own tasks, the default
.RE
.SS task show
.B "wrikery task show T"
.PP
Prints one task: the header fields, the description and the comments the cache holds.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-json
print JSON
.RE
.SS task status
.B "wrikery task status T STATUS"
.PP
Moves a task to a status of its own workflow, by name, case does not matter.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-json
print JSON
.RE
.SS task create
.B "wrikery task create \-\-folder F [\-\-importance L] [\-\-description FILE|\-] TITLE..."
.PP
Creates a task in a folder, project or space. The words after the flags make the title, quotes are optional.
Nobody is assigned, the status is the folder's default on Wrike.
The description is markdown, the text the E editor in the interface writes, from a file or from stdin with \-.
Put \-\- before a title with a word that starts with a dash, everything after it is title.
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-\-description " FILE
a markdown FILE with the description, \- reads it from stdin
.TP
.BI "\-\-folder " F
the folder, project or space F for the task, by id or by a part of its title
.TP
.BI "\-\-importance " L
L is High, Normal or Low, Normal when left out
.TP
.B \-\-json
print JSON
.RE
.SS task edit
.B "wrikery task edit T [\-\-title TITLE] [\-\-importance L] [\-\-description FILE|\-]"
.PP
Changes the title, the importance or the description of a task, one write for the flags given.
The description is markdown, the text the E editor in the interface writes, from a file or from stdin with \-.
It is merged with the description the cache holds: a paragraph left as description_markdown prints it keeps the bytes Wrike stored.
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-\-description " FILE
a markdown FILE with the description, \- reads it from stdin
.TP
.BI "\-\-importance " L
L is High, Normal or Low
.TP
.B \-\-json
print JSON
.TP
.BI "\-\-title " TITLE
the new TITLE
.RE
.SS task comment
.B "wrikery task comment T TEXT..."
.PP
Adds a comment to a task as you. The words after the task make the text, quotes are optional.
Put \-\- before a text with a word that starts with a dash, everything after it is text.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-json
print JSON
.RE
.SS task assign
.B "wrikery task assign T P..."
.PP
Puts people on a task, or takes them off, one write.
P is me, a contact id, or a part of a name that matches exactly one person in the cache, or on the task for an unassign.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-json
print JSON
.RE
.SS task unassign
.B "wrikery task unassign T P..."
.PP
Puts people on a task, or takes them off, one write.
P is me, a contact id, or a part of a name that matches exactly one person in the cache, or on the task for an unassign.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-json
print JSON
.RE
.SS task move
.B "wrikery task move T [\-\-to F]... [\-\-from F]..."
.PP
Puts a task in folders and takes it out of others, one write.
A task can sit in several folders, so \-\-to alone adds one and keeps the rest, and a move out of a folder names it with \-\-from.
F is a folder, project or space, by id or by a part of its title.
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-\-from " F
a folder F to take the task out of, may repeat
.TP
.B \-\-json
print JSON
.TP
.BI "\-\-to " F
a folder F to put the task in, may repeat
.RE
.SS The ui commands
The ui commands act on the interface that is running, through its control socket, and print what it did.
With \-\-demo they reach a running demo, and every value goes as typed, the demo's cache cannot be read.
.SS ui filter
.B "wrikery ui filter [\-\-importance L]... [\-\-person P] [\-\-status S]... | \-\-clear"
.PP
Narrows the interface that is running to importance levels, a person and statuses, in any combination, or clears its filter with \-\-clear.
A person is me, unassigned, a contact id or a part of a name, a status is a name from any cached workflow.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-clear
clear the filter, what F does
.TP
.BI "\-\-importance " L
L is High, Normal or Low, may repeat
.TP
.B \-\-json
print JSON
.TP
.BI "\-\-person " P
P is me, unassigned, a contact id or a part of a name
.TP
.BI "\-\-status " S
a status name S, may repeat
.RE
.SS ui select
.B "wrikery ui select T"
.PP
Shows a task in the interface that is running, the way a jump from the search does.
T is an id, a part of its title, the number or the link from the browser.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-json
print JSON
.RE
.SS ui folder
.B "wrikery ui folder F"
.PP
Opens a space, project or folder in the interface that is running, as from the sidebar.
F is an id or a part of its title, me is My tasks.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-json
print JSON
.RE
.SS ui list
.B "wrikery ui list"
.PP
Switches the interface that is running to the list.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-json
print JSON
.RE
.SS ui board
.B "wrikery ui board"
.PP
Switches the interface that is running to the board over workflow statuses.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-json
print JSON
.RE
.SS ui open
.B "wrikery ui open tasks|timesheet|changes|settings"
.PP
Opens one screen of the interface that is running: tasks, timesheet, changes or settings.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-json
print JSON
.RE
.SS ui refresh
.B "wrikery ui refresh"
.PP
Runs a sync cycle in the interface that is running, what R does there.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-json
print JSON
.RE
.SH KEYS
The ? key shows the bindings of the current screen.
Vim keys and the arrow keys both work, and home, end, page up and page down work beside g, G, ctrl+d and ctrl+u.
Tab moves between the panes, enter goes one level deeper and esc goes back.
