.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The operation is done, a write is on Wrike and a read printed the cache.
.TP
.B 1
An error: no sign in, a name that matched nothing, a store error, a write Wrike rejected, or a token Wrike refused, which leaves the change queued.
.TP
.B 2
A usage mistake, the error and the usage went to standard error.
.TP
.B 3
The write is queued and not on Wrike yet, in offline mode or because Wrike could not be reached.
The next sync sends it, from the interface or from wrikery sync.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WRIKERY_TOKEN
A permanent API token that overrides the stored sign in, keychain and files both.
A command run with it compares its account with the one the cache was built from and refuses another.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Plain output without colors, what \-\-no\-color does.
.TP
.B "VISUAL, EDITOR"
The editor E and C open for a description or a longer comment, VISUAL first.
A command that waits for a window, code \-\-wait, works the same way.
.TP
.B "XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME, XDG_STATE_HOME"
Override ~/.config, ~/.local/share and ~/.local/state, where the files below live.
.SH FILES
The directories follow the XDG base directory convention on macOS and Linux alike.
.TP
.I ~/.config/wrikery/config.toml
The config file, \-\-config PATH reads another one.
The settings screen, opened with the comma key, shows the keys of the file with their values, the full list of keys is in docs/overview.md on the project page.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/wrikery/wrike.db
The local copy and the queue of writes in one SQLite file.
Deleting it resets the cache, and the queued writes go with it.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/wrikery/wrikery.log
The log of the last run, the previous run's log is kept as wrikery.log.1.
A demo run writes demo.log in the same directory.
.TP
.B "The API token"
In the system keychain, the macOS Keychain or the Secret Service on Linux, falling back to ~/.config/wrikery/token with mode 0600 on a machine without one.
.TP
.B "The browser session"
A second keychain item with the access token, the refresh token, the expiry, the host and the app, falling back to ~/.config/wrikery/oauth.json with mode 0600, and ~/.config/wrikery/auth.lock held while it is renewed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wrikery sync                                 # one sync cycle, \-\-full also checks for deleted tasks
wrikery task list \-\-folder "4 Later"         # tasks of a folder, project or space
wrikery task list                            # your own open tasks
wrikery task show "licence file"             # one task with its description and comments
wrikery task show "https://app\-eu.wrike.com/open.htm?id=4552825748"
wrikery task status MAAAAAEPXpuT "In Progress"
wrikery task create \-\-folder Sandbox Try the new command
wrikery task create \-\-folder Sandbox \-\-importance High \-\-description notes.md Try it with a description
wrikery task edit MAAAAAEPXpuT \-\-title "A plainer title" \-\-description \-
wrikery task comment MAAAAAEPXpuT Pushed the branch
wrikery task assign MAAAAAEPXpuT me
wrikery task move MAAAAAEPXpuT \-\-to "Next release" \-\-from Backlog
wrikery ui filter \-\-importance High \-\-person me # narrow the interface that is running
wrikery ui folder "Next release"                # open a folder there, as from the sidebar
.fi
